---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Catholic Context is open infrastructure for Catholic knowledge and Catholic-grounded AI — source-grounded, accountable, and independent."
>
  <section class="section-tight shell fade-in">
    <p class="eyebrow">✦ About</p>
    <h1 class="h1">A modern Catholic library built for the AI era.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Catholic Context is open infrastructure for representing Catholic knowledge,
      Catholic-grounded AI behavior, and measurable theological integrity.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell prose">
    <h2 class="h2">Mission</h2>
    <p>
      Help humans and software faithfully understand what the Catholic Church teaches —
      with transparent sources, review states, and governance that resists popularity-driven
      theology.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Harness interprets <em>Magnifica Humanitas</em> so software can assist without
      replacing conscience or the dignity of the person. The home page opens with the
      presentation film; the <a href="/harness">Harness</a> page has Pope Leo XIV’s
      full address (via EWTN News).
    </p>

    <h2 class="h2">Relationship to My Catholic Guide</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={SITE.myCatholicGuideUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">My Catholic Guide</a>
      is a separate commercial end-user application for personal formation and prayer.
      Catholic Context is the open scholarly and infrastructural foundation it can build on —
      and that others may use without it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h2">Theological humility</h2>
    <p>
      Catholic Context does not create Catholic teaching, replace the Magisterium, exercise
      pastoral or sacramental authority, or claim to discern God's particular will for an
      individual. Draft content remains draft until reviewed.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h2">Open-source commitment</h2>
    <p>
      Knowledge, Harness specifications, Evals, schemas, governance standards, and the
      public website are intended to remain freely accessible and reusable subject to
      published licenses and third-party rights.
    </p>

    <p style="margin-top: var(--space-6);">
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/governance">Read governance →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
